    "message": "fix(upgrade): stop comparing compass versions across two unrelated series\n\n`compass/.version` is written by two producers in two different version series,\nand recorded no way to tell them apart:\n\n  - the release workflow stamps the bundle it ships with the **Ix** version\n    (`0.9.2`), because that bundle is built from system-compass `main` and has no\n    ix-compass-dist release number of its own;\n  - install.sh and the compass-upgrade path stamp the **ix-compass-dist** release\n    they downloaded (`0.3.0`).\n\n`isNewer(compassLatest, compassCurrent)` compared whichever of those happened to\nbe on disk against the dist series. That is correct only while Ix's numbers are\nthe larger ones. The first ix-compass-dist tag above the running Ix version — a\nv1.0.0, or just a v0.9.2 — makes `isNewer` true and replaces a *newer* bundled\ncompass with an older dist build. Same failure as #365/#366, reached from the\nother end.\n\nIt is not only latent. install.sh stamped every install with the latest *dist*\nrelease number regardless of where the compass came from, mislabelling the\nrelease bundle it had just extracted and clobbering the correct stamp the\ntarball carried. A v0.9.x install reads `0.2.0` against a dist latest of\n`0.3.0`, so `ix upgrade` reports an update and would downgrade the bundle.\n\nThe stamp now declares its own provenance and the comparison only runs where it\nmeans something:\n\n    source=release      source=dist\n    ix=0.9.3            version=0.3.0\n    compass=7f98724\n\nA release bundle is never replaced by a dist download — it was built from `main`\nwhen the CLI was cut, so it is at least as new as any dist release published\nbefore it, and one published after arrives with the next Ix release, which\nbundles `main` again. The dist download stays the *repair* path for a missing or\ngutted bundle: that still fires, because `getInstalledCompassVersion()` reports\n`0.0.0` when `index.html` is absent, which no real release number matches.\n\nA bare number is a legacy stamp (everything up to v0.9.2) and reads as\ndist-series — what install.sh wrote, the majority of installs in the wild, and\nno less correct than today. New releases carry the explicit form and are immune.\n\nThe commit is recorded because system-compass's package.json version is not\nmaintained against the dist release series — it read 0.2.0 while dist was on\nv0.3.0 — so the commit is the only reliable identity a bundle has.\n\nBoth installers stop asking ix-compass-dist what it has published. Neither ever\ninstalls from there; `ix upgrade` asks that question, at the one point where it\ncan also tell which series the installed bundle belongs to.\n\nFixes #376",
